// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: @trap takes no arguments
// BUG-882: `@trap(1, 2, 3)` was accepted and the arguments SILENTLY DROPPED —
// the emitter calls `_zer_trap("trap", ...)` with a fixed message, so a reader's
// reasonable belief that the arguments reach the trap output is wrong. Same
// shape as BUG-871's `@barrier(x)`; its immediate neighbour @unreachable has had
// this check all along. Found by sweeping every intrinsic with an absurd
// argument count — @trap was the only one left.
u32 main() {
    @trap(1, 2, 3);
    return 0;
}
